{
  "quest.0D7628ABC6FA8543.quest_subtitle": "Beware of Mold",
  "quest.71CF5F05D0BC692A.quest_desc": [
    "Using Titanium Tetrachloride as the main catalyst and Magnesium Chloride as the co-catalyst, fully polymerize Ethylene or Propylene in the Mixer to obtain Plastic Pulp.",
    "",
    "Every 100mB of Ethylene or 100mB of Propylene consumes 1mB of Titanium Tetrachloride and produces 1 Plastic Pulp; Magnesium Chloride is not consumed.",
    "",
    "To process Plastic without loss, use the Extruder. When smelting in a Crucible, every time Plastic enters the &emolten state&f it loses &cone third&f of its material!",
  ],
  "quest.2050FDF802083E41.quest_desc": [
    "RU is similar to EU, with speed and torque analogous to voltage and current. Total power is speed multiplied by torque.",
    "",
    "Recipe execution depends only on total power, but whether energy is accepted depends on the speed.",
    "",
    "Speed tiers are 16-64, 64-256, 256-1024 and 1024-4096.",
    "",
    "The torque of the Electric Motor, Diesel Engine and Steam Turbine is fixed at 1.",
  ],
  "quest.12BD1323E2EDE6D2.title": "Distillation Tower",
  "quest.769F537543AB2252.quest_subtitle": "Oil and Gas Storage",
  "quest.2050FDF802083E41.title": "More on RU",
  "quest.2C26E493A03BA44F.quest_subtitle": "Turning circular motion (RU) into linear motion (KU)",
  "quest.18A23A99A6672A43.title": "Gas Turbine",
  "quest.71CF5F05D0BC692A.quest_subtitle": "Ziegler–Natta Catalyst",
  "quest.2B7A52C70E91D618.title": "Oil Shale, What Is That?",
  "quest.1CFE23FFE8397318.title": "Catalytic Cracking",
  "quest.5A9E64D6B2253E60.title": "Steam Cracking",
  "quest.6E9947D3BC9FE34A.quest_desc": [
    "Compared with the Liquid Burning Box, the Diesel Engine is far pickier: it can only use Fuel Oil and Ethanol as fuel. In exchange, it can output RU directly instead of HU, needs no long warm-up like a Steam Boiler, outputs more RU per unit of fuel, and even has a fuel efficiency of up to 100%!",
    "",
    "Outputs RU from the front; fluids are input from the other sides.",
    "",
    "While running it produces Carbon Dioxide exhaust, which is output from the back. If the back is air, the exhaust is automatically destroyed; if there is a usable fluid container at the back, it is automatically pumped out; if neither is available, it is stored in the machine's internal buffer, and the machine stops automatically when the buffer is full.",
    "",
    "If a fluid has a “Fluid Fuel: xxx GU/L” tooltip entry, it can serve as valid fuel for the Diesel Engine.",
    "",
    "In the crafting recipe, the Lubricant can be supplied as a Lubricant Bottle or a Lubricant Bucket.",
    "Crafting with a Lubricant Bottle saves 750L of Lubricant.",
    "",
    "It is time to replace the Steam Boiler and upgrade your ore processing and machines.",
    "",
    "&oThere are Diesel Engines of other materials in the game; check JEI yourself for their crafting recipes.",
  ],
  "quest.769F537543AB2252.quest_desc": [
    "The Wood Tank can only hold 432,000 L of fluid (432 buckets). That may sound like a lot, but it fills up quickly. If you need more storage space, or need to store gases (gases can't be stored in treated wood), you need another kind of Tank. That's where the Invar Tank comes in. The Small Invar Tank holds 1,728,000 L and, like the Wood Tank, only needs a 3x3 space. It can also store gases. There are also Large versions of the Invar Tank, but they require far more Invar to make - although they can hold correspondingly larger amounts of non-acidic fluids.",
    "",
    "Likewise, they're great for storing your Oil and distilled products.",
    "",
    "Warning: the Invar Tank can store gases but not acids. You need a Stainless Steel Tank to store acids.",
  ],
  "quest.0D7628ABC6FA8543.quest_desc": [
    "Oil and Natural Gas resources are buried deep underground (at the Bedrock layer), and their traces are usually hard to find directly. However, some special indicators let you roughly learn what fluid deposits may lie beneath an area without drilling a shaft.",
    "",
    "When a chunk has special fluid resources below it, some Grass Blocks on the surface are replaced with tinted special Grass Blocks, indicating that a special fluid is hidden near the Bedrock layer.",
    "",
    "·Brown: Oil",
    "·Yellow: Natural Gas/Lava",
    "·Green: Hot Spring Water",
    "",
    "Dig downward until you reach the Bedrock layer, and you will see large amounts of fluid gushing out naturally. If you remove all the fluid, the entire cave bottom is a flat layer of Bedrock, and some Bedrock blocks are replaced by springs that endlessly emit a specific fluid at fixed intervals; use a Drain or a Rotational Pump to collect the fluid emitted by the springs.",
    "",
    "&cDANGER&f: Touching Oil or Natural Gas blocks may inflict debuffs such as Poison, Blindness and Nausea, and Heavy Oil and Very Heavy Oil even prevent the player from jumping while inside them. Once Oil or Natural Gas touches any ignition source (Fire blocks, Lava, a working Burning Box, etc.), all connected oil/gas blocks will turn into flames in an instant.",
    "",
    "&oThis may help you clear out the Oil left in the oil/gas springs, so you can count how many springs there are in the field.",
  ],
  "quest.1D148ED9C7162496.title": "Transformer Gearbox",
  "quest.45AB3C94DF1E7D8F.quest_desc": [
    "Using a Ceramic Bowl, mix [Redstone/Soapstone/Talc Dust] with [any Oil/Creosote/Fish Oil/Seed Oil] to produce a small amount of Lubricant.",
  ],
  "quest.2B7A52C70E91D618.quest_desc": [
    "Oil Shale usually appears in the form of rock layers; like Bauxite/Salt layers, it is an ore disguised as rock and drops Raw Ore when mined with a pickaxe.",
    "",
    "Refining Oil Shale (ore/crushed ore/dust...) in a Coke Oven produces a small amount of Oil, which is handy when you cannot find even a single oil spring.",
  ],
  "quest.1CFE23FFE8397318.quest_desc": [
    "Under the combined action of high temperature and a catalyst, various Fuel Oils react with Hydrogen to produce large amounts of Ethylene and Propylene.",
    "",
    "Collect some Ethylene and Propylene; they will be widely used in the circuit board industry later.",
    "",
    "Catalytic Cracking produces Ethylene and Propylene faster and with fewer impurities than Steam Cracking, but it requires rare Zeolite Dust to craft the machine.",
  ],
  "quest.71CF5F05D0BC692A.title": "Plastic",
  "quest.286867752CD888A7.title": "Axle",
  "quest.0D7628ABC6FA8543.title": "Black Gold Here",
  "quest.12BD1323E2EDE6D2.quest_subtitle": "The beginning of the oil industry (not a stainless steel block tower)",
  "task.34F72FE1002207E3.title": "Oil Grades",
  "quest.1D148ED9C7162496.quest_desc": [
    "Converts the input RU*T into (1/4RU)*4T; paired with an adjustable gearbox, it can drive multiple machines.",
    "",
    "After adjusting with a Monkey Wrench, RU*4T can be changed to 4RU*1T.",
  ],
  "quest.6E9947D3BC9FE34A.title": "Diesel Engine",
  "quest.2C26E493A03BA44F.quest_desc": [
    "Input RU from the four sides and output KU from both the front and the back.",
    "",
    "Like other KU-output machines, it can power any machine that accepts FE, with a conversion ratio of 1KU:2FE (the 50% efficiency mentioned in the tooltip).",
    "",
    "Note: although this machine's energy conversion efficiency is 100%, the two KU output faces split the input RU power evenly, so its efficiency drops to 50% when only one face powers other machines.",
  ],
  "quest.1FC2DE58F41C1BAA.quest_desc": [
    "Depending on the ratio of light and heavy fractions it contains, Oil can be divided into four types: Light Oil, Raw Oil, Heavy Oil and Very Heavy Oil.",
    "",
    "These four oils are hard to distinguish when they exist in the form of oil/gas springs, and the surface Grass Block indicators show only a very generic brown. You must use a Drain or a Rotational Pump to convert the block form of oil into fluid form before you can easily tell which kind of Oil it is.",
    "",
    "The lighter the Oil, the more Propane and Butane it produces during fractionation and the lower the energy cost; the heavier the Oil, the more Paraffin Wax and Asphalt it produces and the higher the energy cost. Usually, Light Oil is the highest-quality Oil: distilling it takes less energy, and the total energy of all its fractions is the greatest. For Very Heavy Oil, distilling it may be a loss-making operation.",
    "",
    "Soulsand Oil is rather special: it is not produced by oil springs, but obtained by centrifuging Soulsand, and its overall grade is lower than that of Raw Oil.",
  ],
  "quest.5A9E64D6B2253E60.quest_desc": [
    "At high temperature, Propane and Butane react with Steam molecules to produce Ethylene, Propylene and some impurities.",
    "",
    "Collect some Ethylene and Propylene; they will be widely used in the circuit board industry later.",
    "",
    "The machines for Steam Cracking are cheaper, but you need a stable Steam supply and a way to void the excess Steam produced by the Boiler.",
    "",
    "In addition, in the Steam Cracker you can mix Refined Ore, Steam and Molten Wax (Paraffin Wax, Beeswax, hot magic wax...) to mass-produce byproducts at the expense of the main product. This ore processing route is usually called wax cracking.",
  ],
  "quest.6E9947D3BC9FE34A.quest_subtitle": "I like you better than the Steam Turbine",
  "quest.6E519F365E45A460.quest_desc": [
    "A custom gearbox used to transmit RU*T. Gears on adjacent faces connect. Use a Wrench to install a gear of the same material from your inventory into the Custom Gearbox, or to remove an installed gear; use a Magnifying Glass to check whether the gear placement is valid (invalid placement blocks transmission/jams the gearbox, and mismatched rotation directions (clockwise/counter-clockwise) of RU input to multiple faces can also cause a jam (these two features simulate real gear rotation)).",
    "",
    "A single input with multiple outputs can split RU evenly by W; three outputs cause the allocated power to fluctuate constantly, so this setup is not recommended.",
    "",
    "Combine multiple RU*T inputs into one power output; for example, two 64RU*2T inputs can be combined into a 64*4T output.",
    "PS: it is best to leave the input face open for easier inspection",
    "",
    "When the input speed exceeds the speed limit of the Custom Gearbox, the gear on the input face breaks and turns into Scrap of the corresponding material.",
    "",
    "Use a Monkey Wrench to adjust the axle direction; places with only an axle can only be used for output, saving you one gear.",
    "",
    "Known BUG: when multiple gearboxes are chained together like a centipede, there is a chance that some gearboxes fail to connect after re-entering the save or restarting the power-providing machines; the workaround is to use Redstone control so that the later gearboxes are powered first. This is presumably related to block entity loading order.",
  ],
  "quest.18A23A99A6672A43.quest_subtitle": "Unfortunately, there is no small version",
  "quest.2C26E493A03BA44F.title": "Rotation Engine",
  "quest.45AB3C94DF1E7D8F.title": "Simple Lubricant Production",
  "quest.6E519F365E45A460.title": "Custom Gearbox",
  "quest.18A23A99A6672A43.quest_desc": [
    "The Gas Turbine can burn combustible gases and output large amounts of RU; Natural Gas is the most suitable fuel for it.",
    "",
    "While running it produces Carbon Dioxide and Water. Unlike the Diesel Engine, the Gas Turbine cannot actively pump out exhaust gas/liquid, so you need a pipe with active fluid extraction to keep the exhaust from accumulating and disrupting operation.",
  ],
  "quest.12BD1323E2EDE6D2.quest_desc": [
    "Burning Oil directly does not give much heat value. Build a Distillation Tower to distill out the different fractions; the total heat value of all fractions will be far higher than that of Oil.",
    "",
    "To build a Distillation Tower, you need 1 Distillation Tower main block, 71 Distillation Tower Parts and 9 Heat Transmitters in total. Place the Heat Transmitters in a 3x3 shape on the first layer, then build a 3x8x3 structure of Distillation Tower Parts above them, and replace any one of the central bottom-layer Distillation Tower Parts with the Distillation Tower main block (facing outwards). When you see a pattern of 8 round holes on the back of the tower, the Distillation Tower is successfully built.",
    "",
    "Input the fluid to be distilled through the bottom-layer Distillation Tower Parts, then supply at least 64HU/t to the Heat Transmitters, and the Distillation Tower will start working automatically.",
    "",
    "The Distillation Tower has automatic output; all outputs are emitted from the Distillation Tower Parts with round-hole patterns, with strict layer assignment: all items are output from the bottom layer, after which, sorted by density from highest to lowest, each layer from the second to the top outputs one specific fluid. Pipes with active extraction can pump all fluids out from any Distillation Tower Part.",
  ],
  "quest.1FC2DE58F41C1BAA.title": "Oil Grades",
  "quest.4F03BFC5654C0150.quest_desc": [
    "If you have Rubber, it is highly recommended to craft a set of Biochemical Gas Hazard Suit to protect against the toxicity of Oil and Natural Gas; it lets you breathe freely in those fluids.",
  ],
  "quest.286867752CD888A7.quest_desc": [
    "Used to transmit RU.",
    "",
    "Like electric cables, transmission involves some loss.",
    "",
    "Unlike cables and pipes, Axles cannot turn corners; to change the transmission direction, use a Custom Gearbox.",
    "",
    "Exceeding the maximum speed/power will snap it (it turns into a dropped item).",
  ],
}